  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given an assignment from your institute.\n\nEach assignment has a difficulty value between 111 and 100100100 (both inclusive).\n\nAI can solve an assignment if and only if the difficulty of the assignment is **less than or equal to**  606060.\n\nYour current assignment has difficulty XXX.\n\nIs AI capable of solving your assignment?\n\nPrint `\"YES\"` if it is, and `\"NO\"` if it isn't (without the quotes).\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first and only line of input will contain a single integer XXX, denoting the difficulty of your assignment.\n\n\nOutput Format\n\nIf AI is capable of solving your assignment output `\"YES\"`, otherwise print `\"NO\"` (without quotes).\n\nEach character of the output may be printed in either uppercase or lowercase, i.e, the strings `no`, `NO`, `No`, and `nO` will all be treated as equivalent.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤X≤1001 \\leq X \\leq 1001≤X≤100"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "60",
        "output": "YES",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nThe difficulty of the assignment is ≤60\\leq 60≤60, so AI can solve it."
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_2",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "40",
        "output": "YES",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nThe difficulty of the assignment is ≤60\\leq 60≤60, so AI can solve it."
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_3",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "69",
        "output": "NO",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nThe difficulty of the assignment is >60\\gt 60>60, so AI cannot solve it."
      }
    ]
  },
